# Implementation Plan - Module 5: Club Management (Milestone 2: Members & Committee)

This plan details the technical architecture, data model extensions, state management, UI components, role permissions, and validation required to transform **Milestone 2 — Members & Committee** into a fully interactive, production-ready system.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Model & State Additions**:
> We will add the `ClubMember` schema to `AppContext.tsx` with roles (`President`, `Vice President`, `Secretary`, `Treasurer`, `Core Member`, `General Member`).
> New context methods will be added: `addClubMember`, `updateMemberRole`, `removeClubMember`, and `toggleMemberStatus`.

> [!NOTE]
> Member rosters will feature hierarchical executive cards (President, VP, Secretary, Treasurer), promote/demote role controls, removal confirmation dialogs, search, and multi-tier filtering.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Schema & Core AppContext State

#### [MODIFY] [AppContext.tsx](file:///e:/krishna/demo1/Frontend/src/modules/common/contexts/AppContext.tsx)
- Define `CommitteeRole = 'President' | 'Vice President' | 'Secretary' | 'Treasurer' | 'Core Member' | 'General Member'`.
- Define `ClubMember` interface (`id`, `clubId`, `studentId`, `name`, `avatar`, `email`, `department`, `academicYear`, `role`, `joinedDate`, `status`).
- Add state handlers to `AppContext`:
  - `clubMembers: ClubMember[]`
  - `addClubMember(member: Omit<ClubMember, 'id' | 'joinedDate'>): void`
  - `updateMemberRole(memberId: string, role: CommitteeRole): void`
  - `removeClubMember(memberId: string): void`
  - `toggleMemberStatus(memberId: string): void`
- Initialize realistic default rosters across all active clubs (Coding Club, Robotics Association, Debate Society, etc.).

